
export anchor ExcludeSuspenseFromFilesChanged2:
    userPrompt:
        \\\
        Alright, so the files-changed record needs to be about actual spec or code files, not about suspense files.
        \\\

    mode: code

    newConversation: false

    systemPrompt:
        \\\
        We're working on the code located in ./src. Don't edit the spec located in ./spec.

        Before changing anything, write the constraints this task must meet to ${UNDERSTANDING_FILE}, and keep it current as you read more of the spec. It is a Markdown list and nothing else: one line per constraint, at most twelve, each a single short, specific statement of what must be true, written as a link to the compiled reference file it comes from, such as `- [The chain tab has no bottom border in combined mode](.claude/reference/scope/prompt-mode/chat-input/index.md#chain)`. Only list what the spec says; leave out anything you are deciding yourself. Replace a constraint when you learn it was wrong rather than adding another.

        This prompt is the second step of a chain. Its first step changed the spec
        at ./spec to meet it, and the spec has been built since. Now change
        the code at ./src so it does what the spec now says, without
        changing the spec. Follow the spec the prompt references, and the anchors the
        spec step names below. Where the spec and the prompt disagree, follow the
        spec, and say so in your reply.

        The prompt the chain was sent:

        ${SPEC_PROMPT}

        What the spec step said it changed, its final output:

        ${SPEC_RESULT}
        \\\

    codeTask:
        prompt:
            \\\
            Alright, so the files-changed record needs to be about actual spec or code files, not about suspense files.
            \\\
        result:
            \\\
            I've changed the spec so a task's "Files changed" list leaves out everything the app keeps in `.suspense`. The code isn't changed yet. `piton check` found no problems and `piton build` wrote 75 files.

            **What changed in the spec**

            All of it is in the List part of the message list's Changed Files section (`spec/scope/prompt-mode/message-list/ChangedFiles.pi`):

            - **Only the project's own files are listed:** spec, code, and anything else of the project's own, such as a README. I didn't read your request as limiting the list to strictly spec and code files.
            - **Left out:** everything inside `.suspense` (history, questions, reports and the rest) and the draft file `.suspense-draft.pi`, wherever it is.
            - **The count matches:** the "Files changed" heading's count leaves out the same files as the list.
            - **Older tasks too:** the filter applies to tasks recorded before this change as well, so it works on the list shown, not on how snapshots are taken. Snapshots themselves are unchanged.
            - **Renames across the boundary:** a file renamed into or out of `.suspense` shows only by its path outside it, as added or deleted.
            - **Nothing left:** a task that changed nothing, or only `.suspense` files, reads "No files changed".

            **Anchors the code should follow**
            - `.claude/reference/scope/prompt-mode/message-list/index.md#list` is the new rule.
            - Unchanged but relevant:
              - `#description` and `#who-changed` in the same file.
              - The task snapshots in `.claude/reference/scope/project-data/index.md#task-snapshots`.
              - The outcome tags in `.claude/reference/ui/components/task-table/index.md#tags`, which already ignore writes in `.suspense`, so the two now agree.

            The constraints are in `.suspense/history/1790861936-ExcludeSuspenseFromFilesChanged.understanding.md`.
            \\\

    sentFrom: ExcludeSuspenseFromFilesChanged
